Load decks of gf180_n10 against ngspice-45, written by ../load.py gf180_n10.
gf180mcuD's BSIM4 nfet_03v3 as the kit has it (the kit on PATH: $PDK_ROOT/gf180mcuD of spicerack-pdks), typical
corner, its binned models and corner expressions, the mismatch switch 0 (design.ngspice): ngspice-45 reads the kit's
ngspice files; VACASK reads the same models converted by VACASK's own gf180tovc. Run: `nix develop .#testing -c
tests/fixtures/families/gf180_run.sh` (makes ../kit/, then load_run.sh per family; checked). Conditions nom/m3/off,
regions (vgs, vds) cut (0.3, 3.3), lin (3.3, 0.1), sat (1.5, 3.3), bulk -0.5 V; m is the wrapper's parameter on both.
Result: a difference of 1e-4 to 1.3e-3 (w=10u l=2u), the m relation holding on both. Its cause (../gf180_version/runs.out):
the kit's cards say version=4.5; ngspice-45 runs its BSIM4 4.5 code for them; gf180tovc drops the version and VACASK's
sp_bsim4v8 has no 4.5 (version="4.5" warns "unknown BSIM4 version. Working now with BSIM4.8.3."), so VACASK runs 4.8.
The same card at version 4.8 on both agrees to 3e-12, and the flat bin card (../gf180_flat) gives the kit's numbers to
the digit: bin selection, the corner expressions and the converter are exact. ngspice's own AC gds is 2e-4 off its DC
slope in saturation (VACASK's 4e-10). Class: a model version one simulator lacks (VACASK: no BSIM4 4.5), silently
replaced by its converter.

